  "literary_context": "Wisdom comes through different literary forms. Proverbs gives instruction and practical counsel; Psalm 1 uses a contrast between two ways; Job 28 is a poem about wisdom beyond human reach; Ecclesiastes ends with a summary call to reverence and accountability; and Jesus uses a parable about two builders. James 3 contrasts wisdom marked by peace and good conduct with envy and selfish ambition.",
  "covenantal_significance": "These passages connect reverence for God with the way people treat others and make choices. Proverbs 3 urges trust rather than self-reliance; Job 28 joins fear of the Lord with turning from evil; and James 3 describes wisdom through conduct marked by gentleness and peace. Jesus’ builders show that hearing teaching matters when it is put into practice. Wisdom is lived faithfulness, not simply knowing the right words.",
